---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Code Consulting Process for Complex Commercial Projects" description="How Burnham's code consultants handle plan reviews, building and zoning code consulting, ADA accessibility reviews and due diligence inspections to keep projects on schedule." nav="learn">
  <div class="page-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <ol class="crumbs"><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li>Learn</li><li>Building code consulting</li></ol>
      <nav aria-label="On this page"><a href="#plan-reviews">Plan reviews</a><a href="#building-zoning">Building &amp; zoning</a><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a><a href="#due-diligence">Due diligence</a></nav>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="page-hero page-hero--plain">
    <div class="wrap stack">
      <div class="eyebrow">Code consulting process</div>
      <h1 class="h-display">Code consulting, <span class="hl-block">simplified.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">A hands-on guide for every stakeholder in the construction process. There is a lot below the surface of code compliance, and following these steps keeps your project on a reasonable timeline.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--flush-top">
    <div class="wrap stack stack--lg">
      <div class="grid grid--4">
        <a class="card" href="#plan-reviews"><span class="chip">Step 01</span><span class="h-sm">Plan reviews</span><span class="small">Catch corrections before the building department does.</span></a>
        <a class="card" href="#building-zoning"><span class="chip">Step 02</span><span class="h-sm">Building and zoning code consulting</span><span class="small">Clear answers across multiple jurisdictions.</span></a>
        <a class="card" href="#accessibility"><span class="chip">Step 03</span><span class="h-sm">Accessibility (ADA) reviews</span><span class="small">Local, state and federal accessibility compliance.</span></a>
        <a class="card" href="#due-diligence"><span class="chip">Step 04</span><span class="h-sm">Due diligence inspections</span><span class="small">Know what a building needs before it changes hands.</span></a>
      </div>
      <p class="body" style="max-width: 820px;">We apply our code knowledge to large mixed-use developments, historic renovations, universities and schools, residential towers, hotels, business and mercantile tenant build-outs, medical facilities, movie theaters and transportation facilities.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" id="plan-reviews">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2">
      <div class="stack">
        <div class="eyebrow">Plan reviews</div>
        <h2 class="h-section">The earlier we see the plans, the faster it goes.</h2>
        <p class="body">An initial assessment lets our code consultants suggest modifications before the building department asks for corrections that delay the project. No plan is too small or too large; we review commercial, residential, educational, assembly and other occupancies.</p>
        <div><a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact/">Review your plans</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="h-sm">A comprehensive plan review may cover</h3>
        <ul class="list list--cols">
          <li>Occupancy classifications</li>
          <li>Construction type</li>
          <li>Exiting</li>
          <li>Zoning</li>
          <li>Historic preservation</li>
          <li>Site planning</li>
          <li>Energy conservation</li>
          <li>Life safety</li>
          <li>Fire alarm systems</li>
          <li>Sprinklers</li>
          <li>Egress</li>
          <li>Accessibility on-site surveys</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="building-zoning">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2">
      <div class="stack">
        <div class="eyebrow">Building and zoning code consulting</div>
        <h2 class="h-section">Avoid violations before they cost you time.</h2>
        <p class="body">Building and zoning codes are hard to interpret, especially when a team works across multiple jurisdictions. A code compliance expert identifies issues and recommends fixes, so you move forward knowing you have avoided costly delays.</p>
        <p class="body">Our consultants know state and federal codes and are well versed in the International Code Council (ICC) codes, including the International Building Code (IBC).</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="h-sm">Our code consultants will</h3>
        <ul class="list">
          <li>Analyze project plans through each construction phase</li>
          <li>Attend municipal meetings</li>
          <li>Adjust drawings to comply with local codes</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="card__foot"><a class="link" href="/contact/">Consult with our experts</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" id="accessibility">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2 grid--center">
      <div class="stack">
        <div class="eyebrow">Accessibility (ADA) reviews</div>
        <h2 class="h-section">Accessible buildings protect people and the business.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="body">Without an Americans with Disabilities Act compliance review, an owner may not know whether a building is compliant, and that exposes both the business and the people who use it. Our ADA specialists review compliance at the local, state and federal level and provide on-site accessibility inspections.</p>
        <div><a class="link" href="/contact/">Confirm your project’s accessibility</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="due-diligence">
    <div class="wrap stack stack--lg">
      <div class="stack stack--sm section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Due diligence inspections</div>
        <h2 class="h-section">Know what a building needs before you buy or sell.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Due diligence inspections take place before a building changes hands to determine which construction improvements will be needed and what is or isn’t code compliant. Meeting current code isn’t mandatory at a sale, but evaluating existing issues is essential.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--2" style="--gap: 24px;">
        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="h-sm">Burnham inspections include</h3>
          <ul class="list">
            <li>Technical evaluation of municipal records</li>
            <li>Fire, life safety and accessibility on-site survey</li>
            <li>Document and floor plan review</li>
            <li>Code and zoning assessment</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="h-sm">Due diligence reviews may require</h3>
          <ul class="list">
            <li>Municipal records and technical evaluation</li>
            <li>Code and zoning assessments</li>
            <li>Document and floor plan review</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--flush-top">
    <div class="wrap cta-block">
      <div class="stack stack--sm">
        <h2>Let our experts take the lead.</h2>
        <p>Wherever your project is, our local code consultants will save you time and money and simply get it done.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact/">Connect with our team</a>
        <a class="btn btn--on-dark" href="/what-we-do/code-consulting/">Code consulting services</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
